aGatemain_exe   db 'GATEMAIN.EXE',0     ; DATA XREF: _main+242\u2191o
                db    0
                db    0
                db    0
                db    0
                db    0
word_2D4DC      dw 7Fh                  ; DATA XREF: sub_1746E+73\u2191r
                                        ; sub_1746E+BF\u2191r ...
word_2D4DE      dw 0                    ; DATA XREF: sub_102B8:loc_102F0\u2191r
                                        ; sub_102B8:loc_102FA\u2191w ...
aPressEscToPlay db 'Press <Esc> to play the game, or <Space> for the next screen',0
                                        ; DATA XREF: sub_102B8+A4\u2191o
; char msg[]
msg             db 'In the year 2077, the planet Venus was the new frontier for an ov'
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro:loc_10A34\u2191o
                db 'ercrowded, exhausted, and nearly desperate Earth.  Named for the '
                db 'Roman goddess of love and beauty, this hostile world was no parad'
                db 'ise. Colonists and explorers had to adapt to average temperatures'
                db ' of 900 degrees, a surface pressure of 94 atmospheres, and a dens'
                db 'e planetwide cloud cover made up of droplets of sulfuric acid.',0
; char aTheRealReasonF[]
aTheRealReasonF db 'The real reason for mankind',27h,'s interest in Venus lay beneath'
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro:loc_10A8C\u2191o
                db ' the howling wind storms and acid clouds, under the planet',27h,'s'
                db ' jagged, parched, and hellishly hot surface: a buried secret that'
                db ' held seemingly infinite promise.',0
aSomeoneHadCome db 'Someone had come and gone before humans set foot on Venus.  The p'
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro+342\u2191o
                db 'lanet was criss-crossed with tunnels carved out of the crust 500,'
                db '000 years ago by a long vanished high technology civilization.',0
aTheVanishedAli db 'The vanished aliens were a source of intense curiosity and hope f'
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro+371\u2191o
                db 'or the twenty billion inhabitants of Earth.  Wave after wave of e'
                db 'xplorers descended into the alien tunnels in search of advanced t'
                db 'echnology that might have been left behind by the so-called "Heec'
                db 'hee". ',0
aMostOfTheArtif db 'Most of the artifacts discovered on Venus had no practical use an'
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro+3A7\u2191o
                db 'd were little more than curiosities.  The Heechee had cleaned out'
                db ' most of their useful technology.  Or so it seemed until a croche'
                db 'ty old tunnel explorer named Sylvester Macklin found a fully func'
                db 'tional Heechee spacecraft in a sealed-off tunnel.',0
aInsteadOfRepor db 'Instead of reporting his find to the authorities, Macklin decided'
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro+3E0\u2191o
                db ' to try and figure out how to make the strange ship work.  He cli'
                db 'mbed inside and began fiddling with the controls.',0
aEventuallyMack db 'Eventually Macklin found the right button.  Rocket engines ignite'
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro+412\u2191o
                db 'd and the ancient ship climbed out of the boiling atmosphere of V'
                db 'enus on a plume of white fire.  As soon as the ship was clear of '
                db 'the planet, the thrusters stopped and the ship disappeared into w'
                db 'hat we now know is Tau space.',0
aWhenTheShipRet db 'When the ship returned to normal space, Macklin was delighted to '
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro+473\u2191o
                db 'find that he was still in Earth',27h,'s solar system.  He was eve'
                db 'n more delighted to find himself docking with an immense Heechee '
                db 'artifact, a huge space station circling the sun between Venus and'
                db ' Mercury.',0
aMacklinSShipPa db 'Macklin',27h,'s ship parked itself inside a hangar filled with ot'
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro+4A5\u2191o
                db 'her ships of similar construction.  Macklin left his ship and exp'
                db 'lored his sensational new find with a sense of awe and anticipati'
                db 'on. ',0
aTheBadNewsWasT db 'The bad news was that Macklin couldn',27h,'t reset the guidance s'
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro+4D7\u2191o
                db 'ystem of his ship and get it to go anywhere.  He was stuck withou'
                db 't food or water.  He wrestled desperately with the controls as he'
                db ' became more and more hungry and thirsty.  Towards the end Mackli'
                db 'n knew he wasn',27h,'t going to go home.  He redirected his effor'
                db 'ts to a new goal.',0
aMacklinDecided db 'Macklin decided that if he couldn',27h,'t go back, he could at le'
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro+509\u2191o
                db 'ast signal his discovery to humanity.  His death wouldn',27h,'t b'
                db 'e in vain.  Macklin figured out how to detonate the fuel cells in'
                db ' his ship.  The resulting flash was sighted by NASA and a mission'
                db ' was sent out to explore.',0
aTheNasaMission db 'The NASA mission arrived at the Heechee artifact and found hundre'
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro:loc_10CD0\u2191o
                db 'ds of working faster-than-light Heechee starships, a priceless tr'
                db 'easure trove that made the Heechee space station humanity',27h,'s'
                db ' gateway to the stars.  Thus the alien starship parking garage ea'
                db 'rned its name: Gateway.',0
aAfterASeriesOf db 'After a series of military confrontations and a narrowly averted '
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro+578\u2191o
                db 'war, the governments of the major powers on Earth realized that G'
                db 'ateway was too valuable to be given to any one government. ',0
aTheGovernments db 'The governments agreed to establish a multinational corporation c'
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro+5AA\u2191o
                db 'alled Gateway Enterprises (often referred to as "The Corporation"'
                db ') that would occupy Gateway and exploit the technology of the Hee'
                db 'chee. ',0
aTheFasterThanL db 'The faster-than-light starships on Gateway are now used for a new'
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro:loc_10D71\u2191o
                db ' form of high tech prospecting: human volunteers ride the alien s'
                db 'hips in the hope that they will visit other worlds and bring back'
                db ' Heechee machines, tools, and other potentially useful items.  Be'
                db 'cause human scientists still don',27h,'t know how the ships',27h,' '
                db 'guidance systems work, the destinations of these prospecting miss'
                db 'ions are unknown.',0
aForObviousReas db 'For obvious reasons these missions carry an extraordinary degree '
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro:loc_10E07\u2191o
                db 'of risk: 15% of prospector missions don',27h,'t come back and 80%'
                db ' return with little or nothing.  The remaining 5% make the risks '
                db 'worthwhile, and can turn ordinary people into instant millionaire'
                db 's.',0
aYouWonTheLocal db 'You won the local lottery on December 23, 2101.  The prize was a '
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro+6C2\u2191o
                db 'one way ticket to Gateway worth $238,575, including a limited par'
                db 'tnership in Gateway Enterprises, transportation to Gateway, ten d'
                db 'ays worth of life support on Gateway itself, a class in Heechee s'
                db 'hip handling, and an invitation to go on the first available miss'
                db 'ion after graduation.',0
aAWeekAfterYouT db 'A week after you turned in your winning lottery ticket, you board'
                                        ; DATA XREF: show_intro+6EE\u2191o
                db 'ed an interplanetary ship traveling from Earth to Gateway.',0Ah
                db 0Ah
                db 'It is now Wednesday, May 17, 2102, and you have been aboard Gatew'
                db 'ay for less than a day. You have been assigned living quarters an'
                db 'd a proctor to show you around and get you settled in.  Your firs'
                db 't ship handling class starts later today.',0Ah
                db 0Ah
                db '     You are about to become a Gateway prospector.',0
